// OHLCV Data Exporter — copy from Data Window
//
// HOW TO USE:
// 1. Add this indicator to your ES1! 5m chart
// 2. Hover over any bar on the chart
// 3. Look at the "Data Window" panel (click the { } icon on the right sidebar)
// 4. You'll see O, H, L, C, V values for each bar
//
// Unfortunately TradingView doesn't let Pine Script export raw data to CSV.
// The "Export chart data..." option is what we need.
//
// TO FIND IT: Look in the top-left of the chart for a hamburger menu (☰)
// or try: right-click the chart background → look for Export option
// or try: the (...) three-dot menu in the top toolbar
//
// If none of those work, try this keyboard shortcut approach:
// Open browser console (Cmd+Option+J) and look for export functionality.
//
// This indicator is just a placeholder — it plots nothing.
//@version=6
indicator("OHLCV Export Helper", overlay=true)
plot(na)
